{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6e6fkxyxj","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM live bump quota silent drop was hardcoded player color 2","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: Runs 17-22 got bumps probed 0 live despite the Run-22 bump quota being test-green. Root cause: agent._player_position and _bump_player_cells hardcoded the player as ARC avatar color 2, but the live ls20 board (a 64x64 vision composite) has no color-2 cell — the player renders as color {9,12} (the dev program flood-fills the player from color 12 linked to color 9). So _player_position returned None on every live frame, _bump_contexts returned empty, _bump_discovery returned None, and the quota fired zero bumps silently while every color-2 toy test passed. Fix (Run-23): infer the player color set model-agnostically from the ACTIVE program (the cells that change when the program steps ARE the player), cached and program-keyed, fall back to {2}. Also every EWM live config knob (bump_probes, bump_quota_fraction, coverage_persistence) reaches the agent via dataclass DEFAULTS — live_run's AgentConfig(...) only passes game_id/max_turns/synth_llm/artifacts_dir/graph_synthesis — so a future added field with a non-default requirement WOULD silently drop; guarded now by a config_echo in the run summary and a regression test through the real live_run constructor. Separately: the ARC remote API returns GAME_NOT_STARTED_ERROR on actions when too long elapses between RESET and the first env action (slow qwen-coding ORIENT/probe), an infra timing issue independent of agent code.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T13:22:24.993Z","vec":[-0.00873852800577879,-0.0033600309398025274,-0.013492614962160587,0.015046346001327038,0.1121286004781723,0.01027138065546751,-0.0101873017847538,0.032852280884981155,-0.032834891229867935,0.04106210544705391,0.060357484966516495,-0.09141921252012253,0.08249222487211227,-0.016926458105444908,0.023603469133377075,0.0330620147287845